-- title:
--   Disc places are cut out by primes of S₁
-- statement:
--   Let $k_0 \subseteq L \subseteq F$ be a tower of fields with $L$ algebraically closed of characteristic zero and $F$ a curve over $L$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors of degree zero exist, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$); let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $L$, joined with $F_0$, is all of $F$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$, $\bar F$ a field extension of the residue field of $A$, and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with residues in $\bar F$: a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a surjective ring map to $\bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, restricting to $A$ on $L$ and compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has an $L$-multiple lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue. Assume further: an intermediate field $K_1$ of $L/k_0$ with $L$ algebraic over $K_1$, a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ which is the contraction of $A$ (membership in $A_1$ holds exactly when the image in $L$ lies in $A$) and whose elements already surject onto the residue field of $A$; a subring $S_1 \subseteq F$, a ring map $\varphi_1 : A_1[X] \to S_1$, a ring map $\chi_1 : S_1 \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and a set $D_1$ of places of $F/L$, subject to: the image of $A_1$ in $F$ lies in $S_1$, $\varphi_1(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$, $\chi_1(\varphi_1(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$, $\chi_1(\varphi_1 X) = 0$, and $P \in D_1$ exactly when $P$ is rational (the structure map $L \to$ residue field of $P$ is surjective), every $f \in S_1$ lies in the valuation ring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_1$ the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_1 f = 0$. Assume in addition that $\varphi_1 X$ is the image of no constant; that $S_1$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_1$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid; writing $F_1$ for the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$ joined with $F_0$, that $S_1 \subseteq F_1$, that every element of $F_1$ is a quotient of elements of $S_1$, and that $F_1$ is linearly disjoint from $L$ over $K_1$ (any $K_1$-linearly independent family $c_i \in L$ and any $a_i \in F_1$ with $\sum \mathrm{alg}(c_i) a_i = 0$ force all $a_i = 0$); that every valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $L$ and not equal to $F$ is a principal ideal ring; that $\varpi \in A_1$ is a nonzero generator of the maximal ideal of $A_1$ with $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ prime in $S_1$; that an element of $F_1$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it is a quotient $g/h$ of elements of $S_1$ with $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$; that every ring map $\chi : S_1 \to A_1$ splitting $\varphi_1 \circ C$ and inducing $\chi_1$ on residues has kernel generated by $\varphi_1 X - \varphi_1(C(\chi(\varphi_1 X)))$; and (branch finiteness) that for every prime $p$ of $S_1$ not associated to $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_1$ there is a monic $r \in A_1[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ mapped along $\varphi_1 \circ C$. Then for every place $P \in D_1$ there exists a prime $p \in S_1$, not associated to $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$, such that for all $f \in S_1$ one has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = 0$ iff $p \mid f$, and for all $f \in F_1$ one has $f$ in the valuation ring of $P$ iff $f = g/h$ for some $g,h \in S_1$ with $p \nmid h$.
--
--   This is the statement that the centre of a place of the disc $D_1$ on the local ring $S_1$ of a smooth point is a principal prime, horizontal in the sense of not being associated to the image of the uniformiser $\varpi$, and that the intersection of the valuation ring of $P$ with $F_1$ is the localisation of $S_1$ at that prime. It supplies the valuation-theoretic input for [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint), [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.existsUnique_mem_disc_forall_evalAt_eq_of_section`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.existsUnique_mem_disc_forall_evalAt_eq_of_section) and [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.locality_of_disc_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.locality_of_disc_of_smoothPoint).
